          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. Who Should Buy a Zofdim Treadmill</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A Zofdim pad could be a reasonable buy</strong> if you find a listing that passes the
            checks above, the price is clearly below the checked alternatives, you weigh comfortably less
            than its lowest stated limit, and you will use it for walking. In that case the main risk is
            that it wears out sooner than a better-documented pad, and a good return window and a modest
            price limit that risk.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Buy one of the checked pads instead</strong> if the listing contradicts itself, has no
            model number or warranty length, comes from a seller you cannot identify, or costs about the
            same as a pad from a known brand. Buy a better-built machine if you are heavy, tall, want to
